# IN THROUGH A COTTAGE DOOR AND OUT AGAIN (docs/interiors, 21_doors): the coast's
# houses are rooms. The pocket is grown while the player walks up, so the door
# itself only swaps under the cover; inside is lit by the hearth and by the sky
# through the windows, and the window light moves with the hour.
#
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/house.tour --seed=4 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0
#
# Read the frames as a player: 02 and 04 are the same room at noon and in the
# late afternoon, and the patches of sun on the floor must have moved between
# them; 05 is the same room after dark, where the hearth is the light. 07 is the
# room over the shoulder, roofed. 08 is the same coast the player left.
coast calm
village 0
near door:house
await door 5
wait 0.6
shot 01-at-a-cottage-door with door

press use 0.1
await inside:cottage 5
wait 1.0
shot 02-inside-at-noon with inside:cottage

walk 0,-1 1.2
wait 0.4
shot 03-walked-to-the-back-wall with inside:cottage

hour 16.5
wait 1.0
shot 04-the-sun-come-round-in-the-afternoon with inside:cottage

hour 21.5
wait 1.5
shot 05-after-dark-the-hearth with inside:cottage

hold shoulder_peek
await shoulder 3
wait 0.6
shot 06-over-the-shoulder-at-night with inside:cottage,shoulder
hour 12
wait 1.0
shot 07-over-the-shoulder-at-noon with inside:cottage,shoulder
release shoulder_peek
await top_view 3

near door:house
wait 0.3
press use 0.1
await outside 5
wait 0.8
shot 08-back-out-on-the-same-coast with outside,land:coast
